  "conclusion": {
    "actual_source": "All 11 requested Rust source files from the real installed SQLite/Core packages match both fixed Git commits byte-for-byte. The prior 12th primary file is the upstream root Cargo.toml, which is common to both commits but is not an installed member of either subcrate.",
    "original_manifests": "Both actual Cargo.toml.orig files equal their corresponding Git package manifests at 003b698e. Registry Cargo.toml files are normalized and differ by design; they are retained separately.",
    "relevant_git_trees": "sqlx-sqlite, sqlx-core, sqlx-macros-core and tests subtree IDs match at 003b698e and 75bc0487. Only README.md differs at the full root-tree entry level.",
    "package_origin": "Actual two-package .cargo_vcs_info records 003b698e99e024f3621b8043a2426fde5b741171. Future dependency patch manifests use this origin plus actual normalized Cargo manifests and archive SHA, rather than substituting the release tag.",
    "impact": "No changed runtime source/API premise was found for R2c/d/e or the draft native lifetime token. Their compilation and actual causal tests remain unexecuted and separately gated.",
    "normalized_manifest_boundary": "The actual sqlite normalized Cargo.toml has empty dev-dependencies; upstream git Cargo.toml's path-only sqlx dev dependency was not published. Any eventual standalone driver tests must use actual available dependencies/features, not assume that unpublished edge exists.",
    "no_authority_claim": "Source/package equivalence does not establish native SQLite runtime version, native lifecycle correctness, Current authority or B16 completion."
  },
